#: ../../windows.rst:340
msgid "Custom ordinary Fourier windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:342
msgid ""
"A custom ordinary window is a Numba-compatible function receiving grid "
"cycle-frequencies ``ki``, ``kj``, and ``kk`` followed by the values from "
"``len_args``, ``los_args``, and ``other_args``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:364
msgid ""
"Define removable singularities and the zero mode explicitly. Put every "
"physical length in ``len_args`` so it receives the same grid rescaling as"
" a built-in window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:369
msgid "Window arithmetic and its projection caveat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:371
msgid ""
"Windows support addition, subtraction, scalar multiplication and "
"division, and pointwise multiplication:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:390
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Arithmetic materialises a composite ``w_kernel``. Crucially, each operand"
" is already a projected MRA kernel :math:`K_W=\\widehat W\\widehat\\Phi`."
" Thus ``W1 * W2`` computes :math:`K_{W_1}K_{W_2}`, not a fresh single "
"projection of :math:`\\widehat W_1\\widehat W_2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:396
msgid ""
"For exact control of one continuous composite expression, implement the "
"full Fourier product in one custom function or use a built-in composite "
"window such as ``thick_shell``. Projected-kernel arithmetic is still "
"useful for rapid experiments and for quantifying projection effects, but "
"it should be named as such in an analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:403
msgid "Kernel modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:405
msgid "``kernel_mode`` controls how the discrete kernel is built:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:407
msgid "``octant``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:408
msgid ""
"Build one real symmetric octant and fold it to an rFFT kernel. Fast and "
"appropriate for even, axis-aligned real windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:411
msgid "``full_rfft``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:412
msgid ""
"Evaluate every stored rFFT mode. Use it for a real window without octant "
"symmetry, including an oblique LOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:415
msgid "``complex_rfft``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:416
msgid "Build a directional complex rFFT kernel, used by first derivatives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:418
msgid "``complex_full_fft``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:419
msgid ""
"Build a full complex FFT kernel, required by spherical-harmonic multipole"
" windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:422
msgid "``auto``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:423
msgid ""
"Select a compatible mode from the window type and LOS. Custom ordinary "
"windows default conservatively to ``full_rfft``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../windows.rst:426
msgid ""
"``octant`` and ``full_rfft`` evaluate the same projected real kernel when"
" the symmetry assumptions hold. The difference is construction strategy, "
"not a different physical window. An invalid symmetry assumption, however,"
" can fold distinct modes together and change the result."
msgstr ""

